=== start ===
# The NPC is sitting by a park bench, reading an article on their tablet about the drilling project.

#speaker: Player  
Hey, saw you reading about the drilling project. The way they’re hyping it up, you’d think it’s the perfect solution. But is it really?

* [It’s risky. Have you thought about the long-term consequences for the planet?] -> logical_tone
* [Doesn’t it bother you? This could destroy everything we care about.] -> emotional_tone
* [You know, when they overpromise like this, it’s usually because there’s something they’re hiding.] -> argumentative_tone
* [It’s a tough call, but we should take some time to understand what’s really going on.] -> reserved_tone

=== logical_tone ===
#speaker: Player  
It’s risky. Have you thought about the long-term consequences for the planet? Once the damage is done, we can’t undo it. Isn’t it worth finding a better way?

#speaker: other  
That’s a fair point, but what’s the alternative? We can’t just stop progress.

* [Progress doesn’t have to come at the cost of destruction. Renewable energy is the future.] -> logical_tone
* [But what happens when we’ve destroyed the resources we depend on to survive?] -> emotional_tone
* [That’s exactly what they want us to think—that destruction is the only way forward.] -> argumentative_tone
* [I’m not saying stop progress. I’m saying let’s pause and look closer.] -> reserved_tone

=== emotional_tone ===
#speaker: Player  
Doesn’t it bother you? This could destroy everything we care about. The air we breathe, the water we drink—it’s all connected. Can we really afford to lose that?

#speaker: other  
I see what you mean, but isn’t energy independence worth some sacrifices?

* [Not when it puts the planet and future generations at risk. There are cleaner alternatives.] -> logical_tone
* [Do you really think it’s fair to ask people to sacrifice their homes and health for this?] -> emotional_tone
* [That’s exactly the argument they use to justify this. But whose sacrifices are we really talking about?] -> argumentative_tone
* [I’m not here to judge, just to encourage us to think this through carefully.] -> reserved_tone

=== argumentative_tone ===
#speaker: Player  
You know, when they overpromise like this, it’s usually because there’s something they’re hiding. Doesn’t that make you wonder who really benefits from this?

#speaker: other  
I guess. But at the same time, isn’t it better than being dependent on other nations?

* [Independence achieved responsibly is better than destroying what makes us independent in the first place.] -> logical_tone
* [Maybe, but wouldn’t you rather feel secure knowing we’re protecting our environment too?] -> emotional_tone
* [That’s the narrative they use to keep us from questioning their real motives.] -> argumentative_tone
* [You’re asking the right questions. Let’s take some time to dig deeper.] -> reserved_tone

=== reserved_tone ===
#speaker: Player  
It’s a tough call, but we should take some time to understand what’s really going on. Rushing into something like this could do more harm than good.

#speaker: other  
You might be right. It’s probably worth getting all the facts first.

* [Exactly. The truth will become clear if we keep questioning and learning.] -> logical_tone
* [I just hope we don’t regret it later if we choose the wrong path.] -> emotional_tone
* [We owe it to ourselves to dig deeper. Let’s make sure we’re not being used.] -> argumentative_tone
* [Take all the time you need. I’m here to help if you have questions.] -> reserved_tone